Lifetime-SL per yard of concrete. For the same cement loading of
six hundred (600) pounds if the sodium equivalent was one-half
(0.5) percent, then use three (3) pound of Lifetime-SL per yard of
cement.

Please note that you should not use Lifetime-SL in doses lower
than required for a sodium equivalent of 0.6% (i.e. no less than 0.6
pounds per sack of cement). Because some of the Lifetime-SL is
consumed in cement hydration, lower doses could fail to provide
adequate ASR protection.

